## Verification

Planned regression: workflow stage runner workspace caller parses, validates, and
round-trips while absent workspace retains byte-stable hermetic behavior.

Planned regression: workflow default_runner workspace caller is inherited by a
stage and an unknown workspace fails validation.

Planned regression: caller-workspace runner receives the caller repository root,
may commit a tracked edit, and records the post-run commit plus
runner_workspace=caller in a v4 manifest.

Planned regression: caller-workspace runner leaving an unstaged tracked edit
fails the stage before any stage record or gate can be captured.

Planned regression: caller-workspace runner leaving a staged tracked edit fails
the same guard.

Planned regression: caller-workspace runner leaving a new untracked file fails
the same guard while an ignored file does not create a false failure.

Planned regression: the injected provenance seam returning different first and
second HEAD values fails closed.

Planned regression: default hermetic runner still receives the detached worktree,
records no runner_workspace field, and independently pinned literal fixtures for
legacy v0/v2/v3 manifests remain byte-stable and parse successfully.

Planned regression: `run show` JSON includes runner_workspace=caller and human
output names the caller workspace.

Run targeted Go tests for workflow, runmanifest, liverun, and CLI; then run
`make test`, `make lint`, `make docs-check`, and `make docs-reality`. Because this
changes runnable CLI behavior, build and install the binary, then exercise a
throwaway Git repository with: a default hermetic workflow, a caller workflow
whose runner commits and succeeds, and a caller workflow whose runner leaves a
tracked edit and must exit nonzero without reaching its gate. Clean up the
throwaway repository afterward.

## Rejected alternatives

- Failing on every tracked change from the runner would preserve the old SHA but
  defeat the requested ability to edit and commit; post-run committed provenance
  preserves both safety and capability.
- Recording only a warning for a dirty tree is rejected because the defect is
  silent by construction.
- Passing the caller directory to gates is rejected because it weakens the
  explicitly preserved hermetic pinned gate boundary.
- Encoding workspace only in workflow YAML is rejected because the acceptance
  requires the executed choice in the durable manifest.
